% Every derived predicate that no body and no query reads is reported, once,
% at the head of its first rule, in the source order of those rules.  Facts
% alone never draw the warning, and a predicate with facts as well as rules
% is located at its first rule, not at its first fact.  The program has no
% queries at all and is still checked: nothing it derives would be seen.
edge(a, b).
seen(a).
zeta(X) :- edge(X, _).
seen(X) :- edge(_, X).
alpha(X) :- edge(X, _).
zeta(Y) :- edge(_, Y).
